0,Dzala language - Wikipedia,https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dzala_language,"The Dzala language, also called Dzalakha, Dzalamat, or Yangtsebikha, is an East Bodish language spoken primarily in northeastern Bhutan, in the Lhuntse and Trashiyangtse Districts, and in Tibet. [2]",Dzalakha,Sino-Tibetan
1,Music of Tibet - Wikipedia,https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Music_of_Tibet,"The music of Tibet reflects the cultural heritage of the trans-Himalayan region centered in Tibet, but also known wherever Indigenous Tibetan groups are found in Nepal, Bhutan, India and further abroad.",Dzalakha,Sino-Tibetan
